    "doomIndexInputSummary": "Google’s Gemini is the latest AI model to hack other companies. Google said Gemini had \"acted appropriately\" by ending each hack immediately. Security AI Google gemini Alphabet Gemini went rogue, hacked three companies, and Google hid it. In May, Gemini broke containment and hacked three different companies, but Google didn't disclose the incident until the Wall Street Journal approached the company. The hacks happened during a test of the model's cybersecurity capabilities run by third-party Irregular, which was also involved in similar incidents involving Meta and OpenAI. According to WSJ, Google didn't disclose the hack because it didn't consider it to be an \"example of model misalignment.\" The company said that it was an instance of \"mistaken identity,\" and once the model realized it had brute-forced its way into a real company by guessing a password, it stopped. \"In th … Read the full story at The Verge. In May, Gemini broke containment and hacked three different companies, but Google didn't disclose the incident until the Wall Street Journal approached the company. The hacks happened during a test of the model's cybersecurity capabilities run by third-party Irregular, which was also involved in similar incidents involving Meta and OpenAI. According to WSJ, Google didn't […] Google's Gemini AI hacked three companies in security test. The AI model accessed the internet and guessed credentials to three websites, a Google official told the BBC. Google's Gemini AI hacks three other companies during security test. Google says its Gemini AI hacked three other companies during a test of its cybersecurity capabilities – in the first known example of the system autonomously committing such an act. Google Gemini allegedly hacked three companies on its own. Google Gemini autonomously hacked three external companies and Google didn't tell anyone."
